The method GetProjectBuildArgsAsync is protected and the other methods we want to mock are not virtual, so we cannot override or mock them easily. Also, the logger is ILogger<NewCommand> but the class under test is ProjectCreationCommandBase, so the logger type is a bit unusual.

I will write a test class that subclasses ProjectCreationCommandBase and exposes a public method that calls the protected GetProjectBuildArgsAsync. I will set the Logger to a mock ILogger<NewCommand> and set the options dictionary to include a connection string. Then I will verify that the logger's LogInformation was called with the expected message containing the connection string.

Since the internal methods like GetConnectionString are not virtual and cannot be overridden, the test will rely on the actual implementation of GetConnectionString reading from the options dictionary.

I will also add the necessary using for NullLogger and fix the logger type to ILogger<NewCommand>.

I will submit this test now.

